      <h1>About</h1>

      <p>I'm a catastrophic discharge planner at a #2-ranked neuro rehab hospital—where my job is one part case management, one part payer negotiations, and three parts institutional realism.</p>

      <p>This space is for the truth about discharge planning that doesn't make it into the marketing collateral. The gap between what families expect and what insurance funds. The census pressures tied to capital investment. The patients and families facing bad news, impossible choices, and system gaslighting.</p>

      <p>Not theory. Not corporate-speak. Operational reality.</p>
